  pageImages:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 612aeba78f7f69c47bed560f988e191c, type: 3}
  pageScale: {x: 900, y: 900}
  showTextOnMainPage: 1
  showNavigationButtons: 1
  pageText:
  - "In the heart of a bustling metropolis, Detective Lara Gibson finds herself embroiled
    in a mystery that begins with the discovery of a cryptic note attached to the
    collar of a stray cat. The note, written in an elegant scrawl, hints at the location
    of a long-lost painting believed to be a masterpiece. Gibson's intrigue grows
    as she learns that the painting, missing for decades, carries a curse reputed
    to bring misfortune to its possessor.\r"
  - "As Gibson delves deeper, she uncovers a tangled web of art theft, forgery, and
    secretive collectors. Each clue she unearths leads her to opulent galleries and
    dimly lit antique shops in the city's underbelly, where the line between legality
    and larceny blurs. Her investigation attracts the attention of an enigmatic figure
    known only as \"The Painter,\" who moves in the shadows, always one step ahead
    of Gibson, manipulating events to remain concealed.\r"
  - "The climax unfolds during a stormy night at an abandoned warehouse turned art
    studio, where Gibson confronts The Painter. In a dramatic revelation, The Painter
    unveils the cursed painting, an eerie portrait that seems to gaze into the soul
    of the beholder. As the two discuss the true value of art beyond monetary worth,
    they hear the sirens of approaching law enforcement. The Painter slips away,
    leaving the painting behind, and Gibson must decide whether to keep the masterpiece
    or destroy it to end its legacy of misfortune.\r"
  mainTextAreaScale: {x: 465, y: 700}
